<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2013/Short-Hill.jpg" alt="A tonal landscape painting featuring a small stand of trees, a dirt road and distant mountain." width="500" height="320" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">A View of Short Hill, Hillsboro, VA. &nbsp;7"x11" oil on linen panel. 2013.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In this painting I was trying to capture some of the early fall colors that I saw at Stoneybrook Organic Farm in Hillsboro. &nbsp;The paint-out day was heavy overcast and rainy so I worked on this back at my studio.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">My goal was to limit the different areas of the painting to about 4 (sky, distant hills, dark trees and foreground). &nbsp;I left out some foreground clutter and changed the spacing of the trees a little, but the curve of the dirt track and all the proportions are true to life.</p>